WEBVTT

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.620
<i>The war had already begun.</i>

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.950
<i>It's just that nobody noticed. {fsc}</i>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.460
Each and every time I'm tested by sadness,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.460
Kanashimi ni tamesareru tabi

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:33.360
I become just a little bit stronger.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:33.360
sukoshi zutsu tsuyoku natteku

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:39.120
Even as I live this mundane life,

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:39.120
Arifureta mainichi no naka

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:49.330
I keep chasing the endings of my dreams.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:49.330
yume no tsuzuki oikakete

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:53.440
Iriya's Sky

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:53.440
Summer of UFOs

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.820
Iriya's Sky

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.820
Summer of UFOs

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.300
Tired of walking, I looked up to the sky...

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.300
Aruki tsukarete miageta sora

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.770
...and saw a deep blue that went on without end. {fi, fo}

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.770
Fukaku dokomademo BLUE

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.590
It completely engulfed my minute self, {sc, link}

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.590
Chippoke na jibun dakishimete

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.290
 but I still had to move forward. {link, fo}

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.290
Soredemo susundeku

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.890
I miss you so much

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.890
Anata ni aitai

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:30.940
and wish I could share my smile with you. {sc, sc ln}

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:30.940
Egao wo tsutaetai

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:36.080
Because you are here with me, {sc ln, sc ln}

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:36.080
Anata ga iru kara

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.970
a light is born between us. {link, fo}

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.970
Hikari ga umareru no

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:48.740
I send a longing, wistful melody... {fi, link}

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:48.740
Harukanaru yasashii shirabe

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:54.350
...into and beyond the far-off skies. {link, link}

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:54.350
Tooi sora koete todoku no

00:01:54.350 --> 00:02:00.180
And the depths of my heart fill up... {link, link}

00:01:54.350 --> 00:02:00.180
Mune no oku kakegae no nai

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:10.270
...with an irreplaceable and sweet agony.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:10.270
Amai itami michite yuku

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:20.030
Original Translations:
 Lunar, Ayu, AnimeYuki-Spork
 Encode: Jumonji-Giri 
 Other work: ReDone-Subs 
 Special thanks{ep 1 only}: Flatface

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:26.140
Close Encounter of the Third Kind

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.160
Correspondent Asaba! {just use correspondent, no "special" / leave as 1-line due to title}

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.550
Excellent work these past 42 hours!

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.080
Ah, well, you've also done
 your share and more.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.750
We shall meet again tomorrow!

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.930
So today's the last day
 of summer vacation?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.100
Excuse me!

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.980
Grab my hand! 
Your legs... can reach the bottom.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.270
A nosebleed.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.180
H-Hang on a moment.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:15.940
Here.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.150
Are you... sick?

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.880
What's your name?

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.050
Iriya.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.270
Is that your given name, 
or your family name? {would've done first/last, but that's a little too Westernized}

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.200
Iriya... Kana.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.880
You... can't swim?

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.790
Ah, I...

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.190
Can you?

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:49.400
Uh, well, I can show you, 
 if you want me to.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.240
How to swim, that is.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:55.230
It's fine if you don't...

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.900
Next, I'm going to grab onto your hands.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:18.940
Here.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:33.170
They don't hurt.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.950
Want to lick them?

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.490
They taste like electricity.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.400
Let's run.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.380
Come on!

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.980
Time to go home.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:05.020
It's all right. I know him.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:05.550
Who is he?

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:09.020
You could say I'm like her brother.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:10.280
And you?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.990
I attend this school.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.190
And why're you here so late?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.700
I felt like a swim.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.620
I see, I see. I know how you feel.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.920
It's the last day of summer vacation.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.740
I used to do the exact same thing...

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.800
...so I go easy on
 mischievous boys like you.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.340
Excuse me...

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.660
C-1 reporting. Just finished here.
 Will leave shortly.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.270
C-1, acknowledged.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:37.100
Excuse me!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.580
Well then...

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:39.390
EXCUSE ME!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.890
This is the first time you've ever swum, right?

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.080
He taught me.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:48.210
Thanks for showing her the ropes.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.080
I'll have to ask you to leave first.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.610
The people outside 
won't do you any harm.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:04.470
Asaba, did you really spend your entire summer break

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.750
with the club president in the hills behind the Sonohara base?

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.640
Are you an idiot?

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.910
Just take it already.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:13.680
What is it?

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:18.390
I know you didn't do <i>your</i>  homework.
Just don't copy it word for word.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.210
Would you put that away already? And stop doing everything the President tells you{fnArial fscy85}!

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.960
You're a member of the Newspaper Club,
 not its servant!

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:29.830
What, you guys <i>really</i>  went
 UFO hunting? Got any photos? {pics or it didn't happen}

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.320
Of course not.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:35.370
But there've always been rumors saying that the Sonohara base is a UFO base.

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:39.240
Didn't people just see one of those stealth fighters and get the wrong idea?

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:43.350
That base <i>is</i> a gathering point for the Air
 Self-Defense Force and the American Air Force.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.120
The club pres is 
my only source on this, but...

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:48.790
...the mysterious flying objects that have been observed near the Sonohara base...

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:52.550
...are known as the Foo Fighters {no, not the band Dave Grohl founded after Kurt Cobain died}
 of Area Sonohara.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.880
What's a Foo Fighter?

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.880
It refers to a "phantom" fighter jet.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.220
DURING EMERGENCIES,{During Emergencies,}

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.220
THIS ROAD{This Road}

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.220
WILL BE BLOCKED. {What are they, the Onett police force?}

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.060
The term was originally coined by Allied troops during World War II

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.830
...when they saw unidentified flying objects.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.930
But among the "maniac" crowd,
 it's just another name for UFOs.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:08.480
What's your take? {Lunar sure liked starting sentences with "Well," ...}

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:13.280
The standard theory is that they're flying man-made UFOs at the Sonohara base.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.550
They recover UFOs that have crashed, replicate the technology,

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.560
and create planes that are out of this world.{haha, get it?}

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:23.200
So if a war were to break out, those UFO fighters would be flying all over the place?

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.320
Sonohara Area Fourth Anti-Air Raid Shelter

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:31.980
But I guess there won't be a war.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:34.130
Probably not.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.850
You'd never get past 
basic training, anyway.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:39.390
Ah, there's an anti-air raid drill.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.310
Is there even a point to those things?

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:45.770
I heard that the theme 
this time was "realism."

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.280
Iriya Kana

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:07.370
I'm Iriya Kana.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:13.550
Iriya's Sky

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:13.550
Summer of UFOs

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.650
I'm Nakagomi Makiko, the class president.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:30.780
If there's anything you want to know, just ask.

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.090
Where'd you live before? America?

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.130
I heard you lived with your brother.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.750
You both live in the residential area
 of Sonohara Base, right?

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.410
What does your brother do?

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.330
Don't tell me he's a jet pilot?

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.630
That's amazing. I bet he's fluent in English.

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:49.000
Do you help your brother out?

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.600
The opening ceremony for the new term 
will begin momentarily.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:06.770
All students, please proceed to the gymnasium.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:12.040
I repeat: The opening ceremony...

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.640
Wait, Asaba!

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.650
Sudou-san...

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.500
Do you know Asaba-kun?

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:18.780
Hey, where'd you meet him?

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.340
Are you two relatives or something?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.610
I know! They're old childhood friends.

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:25.810
Shut up. Go away.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.760
Way to flee the scene.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:32.700
Akiho.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.730
Do you know that girl?

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.920
I wouldn't say I <i>know</i>  her...

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.490
Then why would she look at you like that?

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:41.440
Beats me. {My animal magnetism?}

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.390
Where did you met her before? And when?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.660
Like I said-!

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.860
Tell the truth already! Well?

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:04.540
Asaba, are you okay?
Your face is totally pale.

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:06.700
Hey, Asaba! Asaba!!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.490
School Infirmary

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.410
Did you eat a proper breakfast?

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.410
Person responsible for fire{in red}

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.410
Shiina Mayumi {original font ABV}

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.990
Yes, and I'm feeling much better now...

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.090
Your name and class?

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:17.610
Asaba Naoyuki, 2-4.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:18.880
From 2-4...

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.610
Asa... ba?! You're kidding!

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:22.220
Asa... ba?! You're kidding!

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.890
You're <i>that</i>  Asaba-kun?

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:28.350
Heh... I see...

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:37.420
The opening ceremony is about to start.
You'd better go join your class.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:42.380
So, you're <i>the</i>  Asaba-kun, right?

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:45.200
Are feeling sick? Are you all right? 
Do you have a fever?

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:48.030
Umm... Is something wrong?

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.850
Take these. You'll feel better
 if you lie down.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:08.890
<i>Come to think of it, maybe that
 summer vacation wasn't so bad.</i>

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.210
Give me a break already! {ita}

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:22.520
You gave him the mist cocktail, didn't you? 
Why would you do something that dangerous?!

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:25.110
There <i>has</i>  to be a better way
 to erase memories.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.180
What shall we give him?

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:30.730
No, I believe it's a difficult choice. {is clear}

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:33.830
I can't be certain, but it might just be flashback symptoms from the mist.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.860
Bottom line is, 
I'm just a school nurse right now.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:42.770
It's ridiculous to make me treat a mist overdose 
with nothing but antiseptic and bandages.

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:45.870
He's sleeping now, but you'd better make sure
 that this doesn't happen again!

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:53.500
The end of summer vacation also means 
an end to lazing around and doing nothing.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:58.180
Thus I ask that you all participate earnestly in today's anti-air raid drill.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:13:59.650
That is all.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:06.150
What about the opening ceremony?

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:08.820
When I came back, no one was here.

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:14.160
Ah... About this morning...

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.850
Uh, I have an announcement.

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:22.710
Iriya Kana-san of class 2-4.
You have a call from Tanaka-san.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.170
Please come to the faculty room immediately.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:26.920
I repeat:

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:26.920
A phone call? {line missed by AnY-Spork here}

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:32.280
Iriya Kana of class 2-4.
You have a call from Tanaka-san.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:36.100
Please come to the faculty room immediately. That is all.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.240
I have to go.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.570
It got even better after that.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.610
Nakagomi and the other girls started crying...

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.200
...and then the transfer student 
got a nosebleed and left her seat.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.240
She should've apologized for 
running her mouth off and acting rude.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.430
She must not believe
 she did anything wrong.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.230
I don't know who she thinks she is. {pan, not sb}

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:03.130
Oh, yeah. Hey Asaba, 
are you coming to club today?

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:05.470
Huh? Yeah...

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.480
Correspondent Iriya!

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:10.800
Club pres!

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:10.800
Club pres!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:13.950
Correspondents Asaba and Sudou!

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:19.290
I can't believe you neglected your responsibility as members to recruit such a valuable asset!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.600
What do you mean, "recruit"?

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.160
That's right!

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:25.150
We, the Sonohara Electromagnetic Wave
 Newspaper Club,

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.560
are a small group of elite journalists...

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:33.110
...that report information from a variety of genres on the spot at the speed of light!

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:37.370
Today, I'd <i>like</i>  to welcome 
Correspondent Iriya as our new member.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.330
Umm, club pres...

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.200
I'll be seeing you again after school, <i>Correspondent</i>  Iriya. {You are in command now, *Admiral* Piett.}

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.920
And give my regards to your brother, 
who's an officer in the Self-Defense Force!

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:54.350
Farewell! Dhaahahaha!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.500
She left the flowers...

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.570
Asaba!

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:12.400
What an idiot...  {sb ok}

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:22.620
0...

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:24.880
6...

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:26.710
2...

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:28.820
4...

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.930
It's WAY too late for that!!!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:34.960
Huh?

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.160
Wasn't that <i>your</i>  proposal?

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:41.220
The new project for the July issue:
 "Ghosts seen in Graduation Photos."

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:44.520
You guys are still stuck on that thing?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:48.020
Listen up. Today, June 24th,

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:51.610
is International UFO Day!

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:56.890
<i>June 24th, 1947 - 
The Kenneth Arnold Event. {no note on this, it's not Japanese general knowledge}</i>

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:02.830
<i>On the anniversary of the first UFO sighting on Mount Rainier in Washington state,</i>

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:06.360
<i>our "Summer of UFOs" also began.</i>

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:21.230
Y-You were on the phone,
 so I couldn't really call out to you.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:26.130
S-Sorry about what just happened.
He scared you, didn't he?

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:29.900
That's our club's president. These days, he's investigating Sonohara Base.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.760
I think he wanted 
to ask you to help him out.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:36.490
You know, since your brother is...

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.510
You see, I'm also in the Newspaper Club.

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:42.480
You know Sudou Akiho? She is, too.{She's the same, too.}

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:46.540
Right now, there's only three of us:
me, her and the president.

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:50.370
Well, basically...

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:53.550
If you joined us, we'd have four members.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.930
I'm kind of busy.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.060
Starting already?

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.160
A drill? Oh yeah. There's a drill today.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.070
An anti-air raid drill...

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:26.570
It's all right.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.000
W-Wait!

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.710
What are they doing?

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:38.380
Oh, we practice "duck and cover" in case there's an emergency.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:39.700
Why?

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.680
Like I said, it's a drill.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.010
They're going to die. {anyway}

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.040
Hurry.

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:12.390
The root code has been changed.

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:15.160
Barrier wall encryption, complete.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:17.680
Disconnecting all external circuits.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:18.880
D-Did you close it?

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:23.340
H-Hey...

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:29.050
The siren just now... I know it's a drill.
An anti-air raid drill.

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:31.230
Hold on to this, just in case...

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:34.100
They might get inside.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.580
It's just a drill! We aren't at war!

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:40.550
The war started in 1947.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.780
It's just that nobody noticed!

